1
00:00:50,544 --> 00:00:53,964
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:59,177 --> 00:01:03,181
Do you have to apologize
because you said something mean?

3
00:01:03,265 --> 00:01:04,432
The sooner, the better.

4
00:01:04,516 --> 00:01:06,142
Apologies expire too.

5
00:01:06,726 --> 00:01:08,645
They'll mean nothing
if you wait too long.

6
00:01:25,245 --> 00:01:26,329
Where did she go?

7
00:01:28,164 --> 00:01:29,165
Where is she?

8
00:01:34,754 --> 00:01:35,880
Is she on the rooftop?

9
00:01:43,221 --> 00:01:44,889
No, it's not messy. I was gentle.

10
00:02:14,878 --> 00:02:17,088
I'll think of a wish, Da-reum.

11
00:02:20,258 --> 00:02:21,259
"Da-reum"?

12
00:02:34,356 --> 00:02:35,357
What brings you here this late?

13
00:02:35,523 --> 00:02:36,733
I came because I missed you.

14
00:02:40,612 --> 00:02:42,989
Ms. Nam, why are you up here?

15
00:02:43,073 --> 00:02:44,074
What?

16
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:47,661
Oh, I...

17
00:02:49,204 --> 00:02:50,872
I came to get this banner

18
00:02:50,955 --> 00:02:53,708
then ran into Director Lee
by coincidence.

19
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:56,711
Please excuse me.

20
00:03:03,885 --> 00:03:05,553
Goodbye, then.

21
00:03:09,224 --> 00:03:10,225
Bye, Da-reum.

22
00:03:14,729 --> 00:03:17,607
Aren't you being a bit too friendly?
After all, she's an employee.

23
00:03:17,691 --> 00:03:18,775
I wasn't, really.

24
00:03:18,858 --> 00:03:20,777
You patted her head
and spoke in a casual tone.

25
00:03:21,277 --> 00:03:22,487
Do you think she's your fan?

26
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:25,448
She had something in her hair,
so I just pulled it out.

27
00:03:25,532 --> 00:03:28,910
We're at work.
I'm worried people will talk.

28
00:03:30,954 --> 00:03:32,080
Are you jealous?

29
00:03:32,789 --> 00:03:33,832
Jealous, my foot.

30
00:03:33,915 --> 00:03:35,125
All right. I'll be more careful.

31
00:03:35,208 --> 00:03:36,376
- Sorry.
- Watch out.

32
00:03:36,459 --> 00:03:37,502
Okay.

33
00:03:43,675 --> 00:03:45,593
EPISODE 4

34
00:03:47,595 --> 00:03:49,305
Oh, my. Ms. Da-reum.

35
00:03:49,681 --> 00:03:50,724
Why are you taking that?

36
00:03:57,647 --> 00:04:00,150
Wait, Ms. Da-reum.
You must be on Team Chan.

37
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:01,651
- Right?
- Sorry?

38
00:04:03,027 --> 00:04:04,529
No, not really.

39
00:04:04,612 --> 00:04:08,700
My friend needed this
for banner recycling.

40
00:04:09,242 --> 00:04:10,243
I am

41
00:04:11,369 --> 00:04:12,787
on Team Ha-gi.

42
00:04:15,957 --> 00:04:17,333
- Really?
- Yes.

43
00:04:20,587 --> 00:04:23,173
Why is the management
more popular than the celebrity

44
00:04:23,256 --> 00:04:24,799
in this company?

45
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:26,593
Right?

46
00:04:26,968 --> 00:04:28,386
- Goodbye, then.
- Goodbye.

47
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,138
Have a great night.

48
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,566
So heavy.

49
00:04:43,193 --> 00:04:45,195
Don't be so weak, Nam Da-reum.

50
00:04:45,695 --> 00:04:47,822
You're carrying your Chan.

51
00:04:48,990 --> 00:04:51,868
I got this. It's not heavy at all.

52
00:05:08,927 --> 00:05:10,011
Ms. Nam.

53
00:05:13,348 --> 00:05:14,474
What are you doing?

54
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:20,355
My friend asked me to bring this.

55
00:05:20,772 --> 00:05:22,524
So are you carrying that home?

56
00:05:23,233 --> 00:05:24,234
Yes, sir.

57
00:05:25,193 --> 00:05:27,195
I'm strong. I'll be fine.

58
00:05:27,278 --> 00:05:29,239
All right, then.

59
00:05:34,285 --> 00:05:35,995
Did he actually leave
because I said I was fine?

60
00:05:46,297 --> 00:05:47,298
Hop in.

61
00:05:47,882 --> 00:05:48,883
I'll give you a ride.

62
00:05:51,177 --> 00:05:52,303
Thank you.

63
00:05:57,809 --> 00:06:00,770
It feels like
there are three of us in the car.

64
00:06:03,273 --> 00:06:05,275
Maybe I shouldn't have hopped in.

65
00:06:05,775 --> 00:06:06,943
It's so awkward.

66
00:06:09,654 --> 00:06:12,407
There's something I must say to you.

67
00:06:13,616 --> 00:06:15,910
Sure. Please fire away.

68
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,081
Actually

69
00:06:21,082 --> 00:06:22,876
I have misunderstood you for a while.

70
00:06:26,296 --> 00:06:28,172
What kind of misunderstanding?

71
00:06:31,384 --> 00:06:34,804
SE Corporation plans to launch
a fashion platform like ours soon

72
00:06:35,138 --> 00:06:36,890
and they've been taking our brands.

73
00:06:38,474 --> 00:06:41,644
- Are you serious?
- Appello's data had been leaked

74
00:06:42,896 --> 00:06:44,105
so I got a bit sensitive.

75
00:06:45,356 --> 00:06:47,525
I thought you were hiding
the fact that you worked there

76
00:06:47,609 --> 00:06:48,818
to infiltrate my business.

77
00:06:52,739 --> 00:06:53,781
Wait a second.

78
00:06:54,282 --> 00:06:55,825
Did you think

79
00:06:56,576 --> 00:06:59,913
I was some kind of spy or something?

80
00:07:03,082 --> 00:07:04,167
I'm sorry.

81
00:07:06,961 --> 00:07:08,963
I'm sorry for saying
all those harsh words to you.

82
00:07:10,965 --> 00:07:12,383
- I sincerely...
- Sorry.

83
00:07:17,013 --> 00:07:18,348
He got me.

84
00:07:19,599 --> 00:07:20,808
How did you figure out...

85
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:23,895
I was a spy?

86
00:07:25,813 --> 00:07:26,856
What?

87
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,614
I'm just joking.

88
00:07:38,785 --> 00:07:41,037
I can't believe you had
such a misunderstanding.

89
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:44,540
It's not like I'm Black Widow.

90
00:07:45,208 --> 00:07:47,460
That's why I'm apologizing.

91
00:07:47,669 --> 00:07:48,795
Please stop laughing.

92
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:52,298
Well, I want to stop too.

93
00:07:52,924 --> 00:07:54,676
But it's too funny.

94
00:07:56,469 --> 00:07:58,930
Don't worry about it, Mr. Kang.

95
00:07:59,013 --> 00:08:01,975
I love Appello way
more than I liked them.

96
00:08:02,642 --> 00:08:05,603
I believe
our company will grow much bigger

97
00:08:06,062 --> 00:08:07,355
and far surpass SE Corporation.

98
00:08:10,233 --> 00:08:12,902
- Do you mean it?
- Of course, I do.

99
00:08:15,029 --> 00:08:18,491
Wait, should I help you find the spy?

100
00:08:20,076 --> 00:08:21,577
- You?
- Yes.

101
00:08:21,661 --> 00:08:24,998
Who knows?
I might catch a trace of that punk.

102
00:08:26,416 --> 00:08:27,458
Sure, I guess.

103
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:29,252
Let me know if you see

104
00:08:30,378 --> 00:08:31,462
anything suspicious.

105
00:08:31,546 --> 00:08:33,423
Yes, sir. I'll do my best.

106
00:08:34,674 --> 00:08:37,093
Who is it?
Who could be doing such a thing?

107
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:40,763
Gosh, I've only seen
people do this on TV.

108
00:08:40,847 --> 00:08:42,098
I'm so excited.

109
00:08:50,898 --> 00:08:52,316
PROJECT OUTSTANDING EMPLOYEE

110
00:08:55,695 --> 00:08:59,907
"Help out
with the logistical task for Go.co."

111
00:09:02,994 --> 00:09:04,454
"Find the spy..."

112
00:09:07,623 --> 00:09:09,250
FIND THE SPY

113
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:10,835
"Appointed as

114
00:09:12,503 --> 00:09:15,173
Mr. Kang's secret

115
00:09:15,882 --> 00:09:17,008
agent."

116
00:09:23,848 --> 00:09:25,475
I mean

117
00:09:25,558 --> 00:09:27,518
I stood in that pouring rain

118
00:09:27,602 --> 00:09:30,646
and worked so hard
on editing the video.

119
00:09:32,607 --> 00:09:33,775
What? A spy?

120
00:09:37,153 --> 00:09:38,321
Jeez.

121
00:09:38,654 --> 00:09:40,782
The more I get to know Mr. Kang,
the more I realize

122
00:09:42,158 --> 00:09:43,451
he's tough to read.

123
00:09:47,497 --> 00:09:49,582
2025 ONLINE FASHION SHOW FINAL REPORT

124
00:09:50,124 --> 00:09:52,043
I'm just joking.

125
00:09:52,543 --> 00:09:54,462
I can't believe you had
such a misunderstanding.

126
00:09:54,796 --> 00:09:58,216
It's not like I'm Black Widow.

127
00:10:00,301 --> 00:10:02,720
What was so funny about my apology?

128
00:10:04,347 --> 00:10:05,932
She always laughs when she sees me.

129
00:10:06,641 --> 00:10:08,810
It may be because
she feels comfortable around you.

130
00:10:09,393 --> 00:10:10,978
Jeez, you startled me.

131
00:10:11,646 --> 00:10:13,689
Alert me before you respond, Luni.

132
00:10:13,773 --> 00:10:14,982
Okay, I'm sorry.

133
00:10:19,779 --> 00:10:20,822
Anyway.

134
00:10:21,572 --> 00:10:23,324
- What did you say?
- It may be because

135
00:10:23,407 --> 00:10:25,493
she feels comfortable around you.

136
00:10:25,576 --> 00:10:29,080
Or she may have feelings for you.

137
00:10:30,915 --> 00:10:31,916
"Feelings for me"?

138
00:10:31,999 --> 00:10:33,000
I am

139
00:10:33,459 --> 00:10:34,919
on Team Ha-gi.

140
00:10:36,629 --> 00:10:40,341
I am on Team Ha-gi.

141
00:10:46,973 --> 00:10:48,015
And?

142
00:10:48,099 --> 00:10:51,435
Do you find yourself thinking
about the moments you spent together?

143
00:10:54,147 --> 00:10:55,898
- Yes.
- That means your brain

144
00:10:55,982 --> 00:10:59,610
releases a lot of dopamine
when you think of that person.

145
00:10:59,694 --> 00:11:03,156
You're in the process of forming
the early stages of attachment.

146
00:11:03,239 --> 00:11:04,574
Congratulations!

147
00:11:05,158 --> 00:11:06,159
What?

148
00:11:06,242 --> 00:11:08,786
No, it's not me. It was her.

149
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:10,538
She was the one who laughed at me.

150
00:11:10,621 --> 00:11:12,415
That's even stronger proof.

151
00:11:12,498 --> 00:11:16,794
A woman's smile is a social cue
and a positive biological reaction.

152
00:11:16,878 --> 00:11:20,173
It must mean
your genes are quite attractive.

153
00:11:20,256 --> 00:11:21,465
Forget it. That's enough.

154
00:11:22,216 --> 00:11:23,217
OUCH!

155
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:26,429
You're really nosy for an AI bot.

156
00:11:51,287 --> 00:11:52,747
I SCRAPED MY KNEES TODAY
WHILE POWERWALKING IN SADNESS

157
00:11:52,830 --> 00:11:54,373
THEN A GIRL CAME AND ASKED,
"ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?"

158
00:11:55,124 --> 00:11:57,627
EVERYTHING WILL GO WELL
DON'T WORRY ABOUT ANYTHING

159
00:11:57,710 --> 00:12:01,380
I'M ROOTING FOR YOU
EVERY STEP OF THE WAY

160
00:12:07,511 --> 00:12:09,722
COCOTALK
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE

161
00:12:33,746 --> 00:12:34,747
What?

162
00:12:36,832 --> 00:12:37,917
What do I do?

163
00:12:40,378 --> 00:12:41,420
Girls!

164
00:12:43,798 --> 00:12:44,966
Girls, I need help.

165
00:12:45,591 --> 00:12:47,677
What do I do?

166
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:48,844
- Why?
- What is it?

167
00:12:50,263 --> 00:12:52,390
"It's the weekend.
What are you up to?"

168
00:12:52,473 --> 00:12:53,474
CHAN

169
00:12:53,557 --> 00:12:55,685
- "Wish"?
- I know, right?

170
00:12:56,769 --> 00:12:58,980
You two also have no idea
what this means, do you?

171
00:13:01,816 --> 00:13:03,359
Why would he suddenly ask this?

172
00:13:05,069 --> 00:13:07,196
- It's clear, right?
- So obvious.

173
00:13:08,698 --> 00:13:10,700
What is?

174
00:13:11,284 --> 00:13:13,286
Namda, make up your mind.

175
00:13:14,161 --> 00:13:16,998
Will you go as a woman or as a fan?

176
00:13:17,915 --> 00:13:20,751
Show up where as a woman or a fan?

177
00:13:20,835 --> 00:13:22,003
Oh, come on!

178
00:13:22,378 --> 00:13:25,840
You're so slow.
What do you think this means?

179
00:13:26,382 --> 00:13:27,883
It's obviously a date.

180
00:13:29,427 --> 00:13:30,511
A date?

181
00:13:32,221 --> 00:13:33,973
Like an actual date?

182
00:13:36,475 --> 00:13:39,812
What do you mean
he's asking me out on a date?

183
00:13:39,895 --> 00:13:42,648
Jeez. You're so slow. Come on.

184
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:46,694
Of course, I'll show up as a fan.
How am I a woman to him?

185
00:13:47,278 --> 00:13:48,821
Namda, listen up.

186
00:13:49,989 --> 00:13:52,450
A fan is a woman too.

187
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,252
Is there a particular wine
you're looking for?

188
00:14:04,587 --> 00:14:07,340
It's not for me. It's a gift.

189
00:14:07,590 --> 00:14:09,842
But there are
way too many different kinds of wine.

190
00:14:09,925 --> 00:14:12,595
Do you know
what the other person prefers?

191
00:14:12,803 --> 00:14:15,222
No, let's see.

192
00:14:15,306 --> 00:14:17,099
He's a man in his 30s.

193
00:14:17,475 --> 00:14:20,561
And he's rather thoughtful.

194
00:14:20,978 --> 00:14:23,898
A man in his 30s
who's the thoughtful type.

195
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,901
Just give me something really good.

196
00:14:27,193 --> 00:14:30,071
By the way, is this a gift
for someone you like?

197
00:14:31,322 --> 00:14:32,365
Yes.

198
00:14:38,037 --> 00:14:39,997
Sir, would you like a recommendation?

199
00:14:40,373 --> 00:14:41,874
- Shush.
- Sorry?

200
00:14:42,541 --> 00:14:44,251
- You should tell him.
- Be quiet.

201
00:14:44,335 --> 00:14:48,089
Wait, if it's for someone you like,
what wine should you get?

202
00:14:48,339 --> 00:14:51,342
I have a recommendation.
This will be perfect.

203
00:14:58,140 --> 00:15:00,601
This wine is said to help
one's love come true.

204
00:15:01,894 --> 00:15:03,604
Help love come true?

205
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:09,902
- Gosh, it's not like that.
- It must be like that.

206
00:15:09,985 --> 00:15:12,071
- No way.
- This is it.

207
00:15:12,154 --> 00:15:14,240
- Gosh, it's not.
- But it is!

208
00:15:14,323 --> 00:15:16,158
You're holding this so tightly.

209
00:15:16,242 --> 00:15:17,701
Well, you gave it to me.

210
00:15:18,077 --> 00:15:19,995
It helps one's love come true.

211
00:15:20,454 --> 00:15:21,455
My gosh!

212
00:15:23,082 --> 00:15:25,251
CAFE RIMONDE

213
00:15:25,334 --> 00:15:27,336
It should be around here.

214
00:15:31,048 --> 00:15:32,299
FILMING IN PROGRESS
BITTER SWEET

215
00:15:33,634 --> 00:15:36,095
Bitter Sweet?
Wait, is he filming here?

216
00:15:36,178 --> 00:15:39,348
I went through so much
just to see Lee Chan.

217
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,683
Whatever. I'm done.

218
00:15:41,851 --> 00:15:42,935
"Lee Chan"?

219
00:15:47,273 --> 00:15:49,150
Is he here?

220
00:15:51,402 --> 00:15:53,070
Why are you out here?

221
00:15:53,279 --> 00:15:55,739
- What?
- Come. We're about to roll.

222
00:15:55,823 --> 00:15:57,241
Why would I go?

223
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:58,868
Aren't you an extra?

224
00:15:59,577 --> 00:16:00,744
No, I'm not.

225
00:16:01,412 --> 00:16:03,873
- No, this is the outfit.
- It's not me.

226
00:16:03,956 --> 00:16:07,168
Man, this is driving me crazy.
We need to match continuity.

227
00:16:08,502 --> 00:16:11,589
Then can you help me out just once?

228
00:16:12,089 --> 00:16:13,257
- Sorry?
- Just once.

229
00:16:13,966 --> 00:16:14,967
Me?

230
00:16:16,469 --> 00:16:17,845
- I'll take that.
- Okay.

231
00:16:18,429 --> 00:16:20,556
Now, stand here.

232
00:16:24,351 --> 00:16:25,436
Please help us out.

233
00:16:28,439 --> 00:16:31,400
Keep walking away from the camera

234
00:16:31,484 --> 00:16:33,068
and Chan will come and say

235
00:16:33,152 --> 00:16:36,489
"I'm sorry. You are not the person
I was looking for."

236
00:16:37,031 --> 00:16:38,741
We're already running out of time.

237
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,701
Let's get it in one take.

238
00:16:41,035 --> 00:16:42,036
Let's roll.

239
00:16:44,246 --> 00:16:45,456
Stand by.

240
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,750
And cue.

241
00:16:56,759 --> 00:16:57,843
Back to your place.

242
00:16:57,927 --> 00:17:00,638
Hey, can you walk more naturally?

243
00:17:00,721 --> 00:17:02,681
- What?
- Why is your walk so stiff?

244
00:17:03,516 --> 00:17:04,517
Okay?

245
00:17:04,808 --> 00:17:05,809
Fine.

246
00:17:06,268 --> 00:17:07,895
You must be nervous, Da-reum.

247
00:17:09,813 --> 00:17:12,441
Just relax and think
that you're walking toward me. Okay?

248
00:17:13,651 --> 00:17:14,652
You got this.

249
00:17:15,569 --> 00:17:16,779
- Okay.
- Take two.

250
00:17:16,862 --> 00:17:18,906
- Let's roll again.
- Let's roll again.

251
00:17:20,324 --> 00:17:21,450
Now, slate it.

252
00:17:22,034 --> 00:17:23,536
- And...
- Wait.

253
00:17:37,758 --> 00:17:40,261
I'm sorry. You are...

254
00:17:44,682 --> 00:17:45,891
the one I was looking for.

255
00:18:04,326 --> 00:18:07,371
What's wrong, Chan?
You got the line wrong.

256
00:18:07,454 --> 00:18:10,499
Goodness. I'm sorry.
Let me do that again. I'm sorry.

257
00:18:12,376 --> 00:18:13,669
Let's do another take.

258
00:18:26,765 --> 00:18:28,934
- Oh, wow.
- Right here.

259
00:18:31,979 --> 00:18:34,148
Seo-jun, are you putting
stickers on his face?

260
00:18:35,482 --> 00:18:37,318
Great job.
Keep doing that for me. Thanks.

261
00:18:38,944 --> 00:18:40,571
Put some more on him.

262
00:18:43,741 --> 00:18:45,868
This is great. I'm so happy.

263
00:18:45,951 --> 00:18:48,162
I'm even happier to see Ha-gi
for the first time in ages.

264
00:18:48,245 --> 00:18:49,830
I'm sorry to bother you
on your day off.

265
00:18:49,913 --> 00:18:52,499
But my kids were begging to see you

266
00:18:52,583 --> 00:18:54,293
and asked me to drag you here.

267
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:57,880
Seo-jun and Seo-yeon,
stop bothering him now.

268
00:18:57,963 --> 00:18:59,715
You'll make
my life at work difficult.

269
00:19:00,132 --> 00:19:02,551
- Go over there and play.
- Yes, go there and run around.

270
00:19:02,968 --> 00:19:04,136
Yes, you can run all you want.

271
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,098
It's okay, Seong-wook.

272
00:19:09,183 --> 00:19:11,685
It's nice to get out for a change.

273
00:19:12,311 --> 00:19:15,022
And it's nice to see
Mrs. Chae after so long.

274
00:19:15,105 --> 00:19:16,857
Gosh, that brings me back
to the old days.

275
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:18,359
When you just started working

276
00:19:18,442 --> 00:19:22,279
you'd chase me around like a chick,
calling me, "Ms. Chae."

277
00:19:22,571 --> 00:19:25,449
And you went around
calling me, "Mr. CEO."

278
00:19:25,532 --> 00:19:27,534
If only my business hadn't failed.

279
00:19:27,618 --> 00:19:30,537
Respect him at work
and watch what you say.

280
00:19:30,621 --> 00:19:33,624
We have a mountain of debt
because of that ruined business.

281
00:19:34,083 --> 00:19:37,586
Please show my husband your favor,
CEO Kang Ha-gi.

282
00:19:37,670 --> 00:19:39,254
- A raise, please.
- Don't mention it.

283
00:19:39,838 --> 00:19:41,924
I'm so grateful for his help.

284
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,135
I should've planned
this get-together sooner.

285
00:19:45,678 --> 00:19:47,388
Come over to my place.

286
00:19:47,471 --> 00:19:48,847
I'll treat you to dinner.

287
00:19:49,598 --> 00:19:52,976
Really?
I'd love to eat at your place.

288
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,603
Stop. What do you mean?

289
00:19:54,853 --> 00:19:56,480
Why? What did I say just now?

290
00:19:56,563 --> 00:19:57,898
- You'd love to eat there?
- No.

291
00:19:57,981 --> 00:19:59,775
I think the kids are fighting.

292
00:20:04,113 --> 00:20:05,155
Is this it?

293
00:20:13,038 --> 00:20:14,248
I can't see anything.

294
00:20:24,675 --> 00:20:26,009
- You found it all right.
- Yes.

295
00:20:26,593 --> 00:20:27,803
- Get in.
- Okay.

296
00:20:36,478 --> 00:20:38,397
- Shall we?
- Okay.

297
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,775
Just drop me at any subway station
on your way.

298
00:20:42,317 --> 00:20:43,360
What do you mean?

299
00:20:44,153 --> 00:20:45,696
- You have to grant me a wish.
- What?

300
00:20:46,488 --> 00:20:47,489
But back there...

301
00:20:49,324 --> 00:20:50,367
Did you think

302
00:20:50,951 --> 00:20:53,328
my wish was
for you to show up at my shoot?

303
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:59,877
I wanted to get some good food
with you after the shoot.

304
00:21:00,836 --> 00:21:03,046
But the shoot ran long

305
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:05,257
and I had to cancel my reservation.

306
00:21:08,177 --> 00:21:10,095
Come to my place. I'll cook for you.

307
00:21:13,849 --> 00:21:14,850
Pardon?

308
00:21:17,269 --> 00:21:19,646
Your place?

309
00:21:20,230 --> 00:21:21,231
Yes.

310
00:21:21,607 --> 00:21:22,900
You mean

311
00:21:23,442 --> 00:21:24,860
I'm going to your place?

312
00:21:25,402 --> 00:21:26,987
Yes, it's right around the corner.

313
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:31,074
What's going on? Am I dreaming?

314
00:21:32,201 --> 00:21:33,494
My heart is about to burst.

315
00:21:33,994 --> 00:21:35,454
- Buckle up.
- What? Okay.

316
00:21:41,919 --> 00:21:44,254
Tech neck, rounded shoulders,
and a herniated disc too.

317
00:21:44,338 --> 00:21:45,714
You're a whole mess.

318
00:21:45,839 --> 00:21:48,383
You should pick up
a workout like Pilates.

319
00:21:48,634 --> 00:21:50,886
Why would a guy do Pilates?

320
00:21:50,969 --> 00:21:53,180
Without this curve,
my neck would be stiff.

321
00:21:53,263 --> 00:21:55,599
My shoulders are obviously straight,
and so is my back.

322
00:21:57,434 --> 00:21:58,519
I'm totally fine.

323
00:21:59,770 --> 00:22:01,688
SMOOTH

324
00:22:10,364 --> 00:22:12,407
APPARATUS PILATES
POSTURE CORRECTION

325
00:22:14,284 --> 00:22:15,452
Smooth?

326
00:22:15,536 --> 00:22:16,870
HYBRID PILATES

327
00:22:18,413 --> 00:22:19,456
The doctor was right.

328
00:22:20,749 --> 00:22:23,377
My neck hurts. It does.

329
00:22:38,934 --> 00:22:40,477
This is amazing.

330
00:22:59,037 --> 00:23:01,248
- This way.
- Okay.

331
00:23:02,958 --> 00:23:05,711
Walking into his place together

332
00:23:06,128 --> 00:23:07,754
makes us feel like a couple...

333
00:23:08,338 --> 00:23:09,715
Get a grip on yourself, Da-reum.

334
00:23:10,173 --> 00:23:13,385
He only invited me home
because he can't eat outside freely.

335
00:23:13,468 --> 00:23:15,387
Cut it out with your filthy delusion.

336
00:23:21,518 --> 00:23:22,686
What should I make?

337
00:23:24,605 --> 00:23:26,189
CREAM RISOTTO

338
00:23:27,774 --> 00:23:29,610
2022 GOLDEN CREST AWARD
BEST ACTOR LEE CHAN

339
00:23:29,693 --> 00:23:30,819
Yes, I remember.

340
00:23:40,245 --> 00:23:42,664
That was the Rookie Award he won
after he had just started acting.

341
00:23:44,541 --> 00:23:46,543
I cried a river back then.

342
00:23:50,130 --> 00:23:51,465
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

343
00:23:51,548 --> 00:23:52,925
You can go upstairs and take a tour.

344
00:23:54,051 --> 00:23:55,844
May I do that?

345
00:23:55,928 --> 00:23:57,012
Of course.

346
00:23:57,262 --> 00:23:58,472
I'll call you when I'm done.

347
00:23:59,514 --> 00:24:00,557
Okay.

348
00:24:01,934 --> 00:24:03,435
- Feel free to relax.
- Okay.

349
00:24:08,482 --> 00:24:09,524
What the heck.

350
00:24:10,192 --> 00:24:11,318
CREAM GNOCCHI

351
00:24:15,864 --> 00:24:17,991
Please excuse me.

352
00:24:25,499 --> 00:24:26,500
My gosh.

353
00:24:27,417 --> 00:24:29,920
This was the shoot
he did with Photographer Yeong-su.

354
00:24:30,253 --> 00:24:31,922
This wasn't in the pictorial.

355
00:24:32,506 --> 00:24:35,842
Am I really allowed to see
these unreleased photos?

356
00:24:38,303 --> 00:24:40,806
Look at his eyes. Insane.

357
00:24:45,227 --> 00:24:48,188
So this is where
he streams live from time to time.

358
00:24:48,647 --> 00:24:50,315
It's so cool.

359
00:24:54,987 --> 00:24:56,363
He's so great.

360
00:25:06,957 --> 00:25:09,376
Does he still make music?

361
00:25:09,835 --> 00:25:12,087
Da-reum, dinner's ready.
Come on down.

362
00:25:12,170 --> 00:25:13,171
Okay.

363
00:25:20,721 --> 00:25:22,222
CREAM GNOCCHI, FISH ROE PASTA

364
00:25:29,021 --> 00:25:32,024
Did you make all these?

365
00:25:33,692 --> 00:25:34,985
You're amazing.

366
00:25:35,193 --> 00:25:37,612
- You're teasing me.
- I'm not.

367
00:25:39,031 --> 00:25:40,323
It's fine as long as it's good.

368
00:25:41,033 --> 00:25:44,077
I tried doing my best,
but I don't know how good it is.

369
00:25:46,496 --> 00:25:47,497
Thank you.

370
00:25:54,254 --> 00:25:55,672
It's really good.

371
00:25:56,965 --> 00:25:58,508
It's like a dish
made by a famous chef.

372
00:25:58,592 --> 00:26:01,011
Really? I did get some help.

373
00:26:01,803 --> 00:26:03,889
Eat up, Da-reum. Here.

374
00:26:04,473 --> 00:26:05,599
Thank you.

375
00:26:12,522 --> 00:26:15,358
I'm too nervous
to enjoy this right now.

376
00:26:16,193 --> 00:26:17,903
I hope you weren't lying
when you said it was good.

377
00:26:21,114 --> 00:26:24,076
I'm just a bit nervous.

378
00:26:25,035 --> 00:26:27,996
- If it's too much, just leave it.
- No, it's not.

379
00:26:28,413 --> 00:26:31,166
Usually, I would've finished
all of these in three minutes.

380
00:26:34,503 --> 00:26:35,545
One second.

381
00:26:47,724 --> 00:26:49,935
YOON CHO-YI

382
00:26:59,903 --> 00:27:01,321
How's work?

383
00:27:04,699 --> 00:27:06,243
It's probably not easy
to work with Ha-gi.

384
00:27:09,704 --> 00:27:10,997
It's not.

385
00:27:11,623 --> 00:27:13,208
When he comes next to me

386
00:27:13,750 --> 00:27:15,710
I get chills down my spine.

387
00:27:17,254 --> 00:27:19,381
He's someone
I can't seem to get close to.

388
00:27:19,881 --> 00:27:21,007
He's like that.

389
00:27:21,174 --> 00:27:24,136
He never lets his guard down
around people.

390
00:27:24,219 --> 00:27:26,471
Yes, exactly.

391
00:27:26,805 --> 00:27:30,642
His office is impeccably neat
right down to every single pen.

392
00:27:31,101 --> 00:27:33,019
He's probably like that at home too.

393
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:34,563
Right?

394
00:27:43,321 --> 00:27:44,865
Hey, this is really good.

395
00:27:45,407 --> 00:27:46,533
Eat up.

396
00:27:47,534 --> 00:27:49,119
- Go.
- Let's go.

397
00:27:49,911 --> 00:27:52,205
- Guys, no running.
- Don't you love his place?

398
00:27:52,289 --> 00:27:53,623
This isn't our place!

399
00:27:53,707 --> 00:27:54,958
- I wish it were.
- Hey.

400
00:27:55,041 --> 00:27:56,835
The one thing Ha-gi can't stand

401
00:27:57,335 --> 00:27:59,171
is anything
that's hectic and disorderly.

402
00:27:59,588 --> 00:28:01,464
He rarely ever invites people over.

403
00:28:01,715 --> 00:28:03,008
Sorry, Ha-gi.

404
00:28:03,758 --> 00:28:05,677
- It's okay.
- Stop running!

405
00:28:06,928 --> 00:28:08,013
What's this?

406
00:28:09,264 --> 00:28:11,308
- But one funny thing about him.
- Hey! No!

407
00:28:14,060 --> 00:28:15,562
- Uncle Ha-gi...
- Uncle Ha-gi...

408
00:28:21,318 --> 00:28:22,360
Fine.

409
00:28:23,612 --> 00:28:25,030
Go ahead.

410
00:28:31,411 --> 00:28:33,997
He has the weakest spot
for people within his boundary.

411
00:28:36,666 --> 00:28:38,877
He was really nosy when we were kids.

412
00:28:39,336 --> 00:28:40,462
You mean, Mr. Kang?

413
00:28:41,213 --> 00:28:42,422
That's hard to imagine.

414
00:28:44,341 --> 00:28:47,260
The reason we got close
was thanks to his nosiness.

415
00:28:48,428 --> 00:28:50,597
I wasn't looking to make friends

416
00:28:50,972 --> 00:28:52,098
but Ha-gi

417
00:28:52,891 --> 00:28:54,392
kept pestering me.

418
00:28:56,269 --> 00:28:57,938
I transferred
when I was in 10th grade

419
00:28:58,647 --> 00:29:00,023
and had trouble adapting.

420
00:29:00,982 --> 00:29:01,983
I got bullied too.

421
00:29:03,944 --> 00:29:05,904
- There you are, my friend.
- What?

422
00:29:06,821 --> 00:29:07,822
What are you doing?

423
00:29:07,906 --> 00:29:09,157
Time to pay
this week's friendship fee.

424
00:29:09,407 --> 00:29:10,492
Cut it out.

425
00:29:12,702 --> 00:29:13,703
Thanks a lot.

426
00:29:17,165 --> 00:29:18,333
Oh, sorry.

427
00:29:18,541 --> 00:29:20,168
He's a player on my team.

428
00:29:20,377 --> 00:29:22,003
Do you have business with him?

429
00:29:23,296 --> 00:29:24,798
Darn it.

430
00:29:24,881 --> 00:29:27,425
Ha-gi was the school president,
who got good grades

431
00:29:27,509 --> 00:29:29,552
and was good at basketball.
The typical golden boy.

432
00:29:29,636 --> 00:29:30,637
Let's go.

433
00:29:32,389 --> 00:29:33,556
I'll get you later.

434
00:29:42,065 --> 00:29:43,066
Hey.

435
00:29:44,401 --> 00:29:46,319
We really need
more players on our team.

436
00:29:47,028 --> 00:29:48,196
Can you play one game with us?

437
00:29:49,114 --> 00:29:50,115
What?

438
00:29:51,241 --> 00:29:53,201
- Come on.
- Let's split into teams.

439
00:29:53,285 --> 00:29:54,619
- Okay.
- Come on.

440
00:29:54,703 --> 00:29:56,788
The losers treat the winners
to snacks at the snack bar.

441
00:29:57,122 --> 00:29:58,957
- Let's go.
- Come on.

442
00:30:09,342 --> 00:30:10,385
Hey, Chan.

443
00:30:10,969 --> 00:30:11,970
Time for a snack bar run.

444
00:30:16,725 --> 00:30:17,726
Hey.

445
00:30:18,518 --> 00:30:19,894
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

446
00:30:20,854 --> 00:30:21,896
What?

447
00:30:22,439 --> 00:30:25,525
- Come on.
- And he was a warm-hearted kid

448
00:30:25,775 --> 00:30:27,652
who couldn't see anyone get left out.

449
00:30:32,449 --> 00:30:33,950
- Go, Ha-gi.
- Go, Ha-gi.

450
00:30:34,242 --> 00:30:36,453
Over here!

451
00:30:36,536 --> 00:30:39,205
- Nice job!
- Oh, no.

452
00:30:40,540 --> 00:30:41,916
You got this, Ha-gi.

453
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,418
Just do your thing. Yes.

454
00:30:43,668 --> 00:30:44,919
Yes, that's it.

455
00:30:45,295 --> 00:30:47,339
- Nice job!
- Okay!

456
00:30:47,964 --> 00:30:49,257
Great job!

457
00:30:51,926 --> 00:30:53,219
Nice job!

458
00:30:53,303 --> 00:30:55,180
That was awesome, Ha-gi!

459
00:30:55,263 --> 00:30:56,973
- Awesome job.
- Let's go.

460
00:30:59,434 --> 00:31:01,978
Thanks to him,
I gradually changed too.

461
00:31:03,146 --> 00:31:05,732
- Hey, wait.
- Let's go!

462
00:31:06,232 --> 00:31:07,442
What do you want to eat?

463
00:31:07,859 --> 00:31:09,069
What do you feel like?

464
00:31:09,152 --> 00:31:10,570
It was a lot of fun

465
00:31:10,779 --> 00:31:13,239
- to spend time with Ha-gi.
- I don't know. What should we eat?

466
00:31:13,990 --> 00:31:16,284
I even stuck around at his place
and had dinner every day.

467
00:31:16,368 --> 00:31:17,452
It smells great.

468
00:31:17,702 --> 00:31:20,080
- My parents always came home late.
- Thank you.

469
00:31:20,163 --> 00:31:21,498
Thank you.

470
00:31:21,873 --> 00:31:23,041
Hey, you made bulgogi.

471
00:31:23,124 --> 00:31:24,834
Yes, because it's your favorite.

472
00:31:39,849 --> 00:31:40,850
Eat up.

473
00:31:48,441 --> 00:31:49,901
Just as you helped me

474
00:31:51,194 --> 00:31:53,071
overcome my darkest times

475
00:31:54,697 --> 00:31:56,908
you had Mr. Kang with you.

476
00:31:58,660 --> 00:31:59,786
He is

477
00:32:00,578 --> 00:32:02,664
my one and only friend.

478
00:32:05,083 --> 00:32:07,460
Maybe everyone wanted
to be friends with you

479
00:32:07,544 --> 00:32:09,671
but you just didn't realize it?

480
00:32:10,255 --> 00:32:12,298
No way. I wasn't that popular.

481
00:32:13,466 --> 00:32:15,176
- You're lying.
- I'm serious.

482
00:32:15,677 --> 00:32:17,262
Ha-gi was much more popular.

483
00:32:17,804 --> 00:32:18,805
Really?

484
00:32:20,181 --> 00:32:22,016
I guess it shows

485
00:32:23,893 --> 00:32:26,020
whether a person
has always been loved

486
00:32:29,524 --> 00:32:30,733
or they haven't.

487
00:32:38,366 --> 00:32:40,201
Everyone leaves me in the end.

488
00:32:42,579 --> 00:32:43,705
I wouldn't.

489
00:32:44,706 --> 00:32:46,458
For the last ten years... No.

490
00:32:47,125 --> 00:32:48,168
To be exact

491
00:32:49,043 --> 00:32:51,463
I've liked only you
for the last 11 years and ten months.

492
00:32:51,546 --> 00:32:53,965
I have never set my eyes
on anyone else, not even once.

493
00:32:54,048 --> 00:32:56,718
And I will continue to like only you.

494
00:33:01,264 --> 00:33:04,267
Wait, what have I done just now?

495
00:33:04,976 --> 00:33:08,062
Look how overwhelmed he is.

496
00:33:09,063 --> 00:33:10,190
I mean

497
00:33:11,274 --> 00:33:12,317
as a fan.

498
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,860
Completely as a fan.

499
00:33:14,360 --> 00:33:16,488
Just as a fan.

500
00:33:30,293 --> 00:33:31,419
Thanks for liking me.

501
00:33:33,296 --> 00:33:34,631
I'm not even a big deal

502
00:33:35,715 --> 00:33:38,051
but thank you for your support
over such a long time.

503
00:33:38,426 --> 00:33:39,511
Thank you.

504
00:33:39,886 --> 00:33:41,513
I want to thank you too.

505
00:33:43,556 --> 00:33:47,560
And I never thought
I'd see a day like this in my life.

506
00:33:49,646 --> 00:33:50,647
Da-reum.

507
00:33:51,064 --> 00:33:52,273
Can I ask you for a favor?

508
00:34:16,631 --> 00:34:17,840
What do you think about this song?

509
00:34:19,717 --> 00:34:21,010
I love it.

510
00:34:22,011 --> 00:34:25,515
It reminds me of old D.N.X songs.

511
00:34:28,142 --> 00:34:29,394
D.N.X.

512
00:34:30,979 --> 00:34:33,565
I only meant how the song sounded.

513
00:34:35,483 --> 00:34:36,568
I'm sorry.

514
00:34:36,734 --> 00:34:38,194
I shouldn't have brought it up.

515
00:34:38,278 --> 00:34:39,612
No, don't say that.

516
00:34:40,905 --> 00:34:42,365
I'm so grateful

517
00:34:42,740 --> 00:34:44,701
that you still think about D.N.X.

518
00:34:49,497 --> 00:34:50,540
Da-reum.

519
00:34:52,542 --> 00:34:54,502
Do you also want us to reunite?

520
00:34:55,837 --> 00:34:57,088
Yes, of course.

521
00:34:57,463 --> 00:34:59,591
All D-Angels would feel the same.

522
00:35:01,926 --> 00:35:04,512
It's actually meant
to be a D.N.X fan song.

523
00:35:06,764 --> 00:35:08,600
If we ever reunite

524
00:35:09,142 --> 00:35:10,518
I want to sing it with everyone.

525
00:35:12,645 --> 00:35:13,688
Chan...

526
00:35:14,564 --> 00:35:16,149
I also did the mixing.
Would you like to listen to it?

527
00:35:16,232 --> 00:35:18,109
Oh, yes. I'd love to listen to it.

528
00:35:35,084 --> 00:35:36,169
What's this?

529
00:35:37,045 --> 00:35:38,171
What is this vibe?

530
00:35:44,927 --> 00:35:47,430
You're so slow.
What do you think this means?

531
00:35:47,639 --> 00:35:49,641
It's obviously a date.

532
00:35:49,849 --> 00:35:51,559
A fan is a woman too.

533
00:35:52,685 --> 00:35:53,895
What do I do?

534
00:36:09,327 --> 00:36:10,328
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

535
00:36:20,171 --> 00:36:21,547
What are you guys doing?

536
00:36:27,053 --> 00:36:28,179
What are you doing here?

537
00:36:28,930 --> 00:36:30,640
Am I in the wrong place?

538
00:36:33,476 --> 00:36:34,894
Is it you this time?

539
00:36:35,436 --> 00:36:36,896
How was the fan meet with him?

540
00:36:37,563 --> 00:36:39,107
Did you enjoy it
to your heart's content?

541
00:36:39,899 --> 00:36:41,901
- Pardon?
- Come out. Let's talk outside.

542
00:36:43,027 --> 00:36:44,028
Did I

543
00:36:44,612 --> 00:36:47,031
walk in
when you were expecting something?

544
00:36:47,115 --> 00:36:48,116
Hey, Yoon Cho-yi.

545
00:36:53,413 --> 00:36:55,790
Oh, no. I guess I was right.

546
00:36:57,959 --> 00:37:00,128
Did you really think
there was something going on?

547
00:37:04,173 --> 00:37:06,926
- She's cute.
- What are you saying? Get out.

548
00:37:07,635 --> 00:37:09,512
No, I'll leave.

549
00:37:14,267 --> 00:37:15,768
Thank you for everything today,
Director Lee.

550
00:37:15,977 --> 00:37:18,187
I'm sorry, but if you don't mind,
I'll get going first.

551
00:37:19,105 --> 00:37:20,148
Da-reum.

552
00:37:25,027 --> 00:37:26,070
Da-reum.

553
00:37:36,038 --> 00:37:37,039
Da-reum.

554
00:37:47,467 --> 00:37:49,510
Chan, I'm sorry.

555
00:37:49,886 --> 00:37:51,512
I was such a bother today.

556
00:37:52,138 --> 00:37:53,431
You should get inside.

557
00:37:53,514 --> 00:37:56,142
- Da-reum, that's not it...
- Chan.

558
00:37:56,726 --> 00:37:57,769
Can you

559
00:37:58,978 --> 00:38:01,105
just let me go?

560
00:38:02,398 --> 00:38:03,441
I feel

561
00:38:05,943 --> 00:38:07,737
mortified right now.

562
00:38:48,694 --> 00:38:50,822
Why did I dress up?

563
00:38:52,990 --> 00:38:54,242
This is humiliating.

564
00:39:21,310 --> 00:39:22,603
How did you get in?

565
00:39:24,981 --> 00:39:27,191
The passcode to your door is
still the same.

566
00:39:28,860 --> 00:39:30,778
You must've kept it
because you wanted me to come in.

567
00:39:33,781 --> 00:39:35,116
The person who was just here...

568
00:39:36,158 --> 00:39:38,744
I had her over for a meal
because she was a special fan.

569
00:39:40,246 --> 00:39:42,290
She's not someone
you can talk to like that.

570
00:39:42,540 --> 00:39:45,376
Have you ever had me over
for anything when we were dating?

571
00:39:45,918 --> 00:39:47,086
What does she mean to you?

572
00:39:47,169 --> 00:39:48,838
Why are you treating her
like she's special?

573
00:39:48,921 --> 00:39:52,216
She rooted for me for ten years,
but I've never done anything for her.

574
00:39:53,676 --> 00:39:54,677
Right.

575
00:39:54,927 --> 00:39:56,637
You have always been like that.

576
00:39:56,888 --> 00:39:59,432
You act like a good person
on the outside.

577
00:40:00,099 --> 00:40:02,643
You think you won't hurt other people
like you hurt me?

578
00:40:03,269 --> 00:40:05,021
Whoever you choose to date

579
00:40:05,688 --> 00:40:06,731
you'll still be the same.

580
00:40:11,611 --> 00:40:14,280
Ha-gi, thanks for everything today.
See you next time.

581
00:40:14,363 --> 00:40:15,656
- Bye.
- Say bye to Uncle Ha-gi.

582
00:40:15,740 --> 00:40:17,033
- Bye.
- Bye, Uncle Ha-gi.

583
00:40:17,116 --> 00:40:18,576
See you.

584
00:40:18,659 --> 00:40:20,620
- Bye.
- Take care.

585
00:40:20,703 --> 00:40:23,831
See you. Bye.

586
00:40:32,715 --> 00:40:34,425
A sticker remover.

587
00:40:36,302 --> 00:40:37,303
Where can I get it?

588
00:40:48,606 --> 00:40:50,733
BEAUTY TRIO GROUP CHAT

589
00:40:51,317 --> 00:40:54,195
Namda! Are you still with Chan?

590
00:40:54,278 --> 00:40:56,781
Are you alive or not?
Why aren't you answering?

591
00:41:05,915 --> 00:41:08,501
BITTER SWEET

592
00:41:10,419 --> 00:41:14,298
I hope they aren't fighting
because of me.

593
00:41:16,550 --> 00:41:17,677
I doubt it.

594
00:41:18,386 --> 00:41:19,553
I mean nothing to them.

595
00:41:21,806 --> 00:41:26,894
BITTER SWEET

596
00:41:29,772 --> 00:41:32,066
Oh, no. I guess I was right.

597
00:41:32,900 --> 00:41:35,027
Did you really think
there was something going on?

598
00:41:39,907 --> 00:41:41,200
This is humiliating.

599
00:41:42,493 --> 00:41:44,537
Come to your senses, Nam Da-reum.

600
00:41:45,413 --> 00:41:47,665
You're just one of his numerous fans.

601
00:42:16,444 --> 00:42:20,656
INCOMING CALL
CHAN

602
00:42:37,214 --> 00:42:38,799
Where on earth can I get it?

603
00:43:02,782 --> 00:43:03,783
Wait...

604
00:43:23,219 --> 00:43:24,220
Ms. Nam!

605
00:43:45,199 --> 00:43:46,200
Are you okay?

606
00:43:47,868 --> 00:43:48,869
Yes.

607
00:43:56,085 --> 00:43:57,461
Why aren't you watching
where you're going?

608
00:43:57,837 --> 00:43:59,880
Why did you cross the road
without checking the traffic light?

609
00:44:05,302 --> 00:44:06,387
I'm sorry.

610
00:44:09,431 --> 00:44:11,642
I couldn't see it.

611
00:44:14,353 --> 00:44:15,396
I really

612
00:44:16,605 --> 00:44:18,232
didn't see it.

613
00:44:23,237 --> 00:44:25,030
I know I was wrong.

614
00:44:26,907 --> 00:44:29,743
If you yell at me like that

615
00:44:33,581 --> 00:44:35,749
I don't know what to say.

616
00:44:52,558 --> 00:44:53,684
Sorry for getting mad at you.

617
00:44:55,019 --> 00:44:56,020
I was startled too.

618
00:44:58,522 --> 00:45:01,066
No, I'm sorry.

619
00:45:02,193 --> 00:45:03,235
Did

620
00:45:04,278 --> 00:45:05,279
something bad happen?

621
00:45:08,782 --> 00:45:09,825
No.

622
00:45:10,451 --> 00:45:13,162
Today was
the happiest day of my life.

623
00:45:18,834 --> 00:45:19,877
Something

624
00:45:21,212 --> 00:45:23,130
I'd always dreamed of
happened to me.

625
00:45:25,424 --> 00:45:26,467
But

626
00:45:27,885 --> 00:45:31,180
I didn't realize dreams end...

627
00:45:34,475 --> 00:45:35,476
once I wake up.

628
00:45:49,615 --> 00:45:50,616
Let's go.

629
00:45:51,158 --> 00:45:52,201
I'll take you home.

630
00:45:53,035 --> 00:45:54,036
Okay.

631
00:45:57,623 --> 00:45:58,624
Your bag.

632
00:45:59,124 --> 00:46:00,125
Oh, that's right.

633
00:46:05,673 --> 00:46:06,799
What's wrong with me?

634
00:46:17,184 --> 00:46:18,185
INKUK HOSPITAL

635
00:46:18,269 --> 00:46:19,311
You sprained your ligament.

636
00:46:19,979 --> 00:46:21,772
You need to wear it
for at least two weeks.

637
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:43,961
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

638
00:46:48,799 --> 00:46:51,969
These are what I could find for now.
I thought you might need them.

639
00:46:54,096 --> 00:46:55,139
What are they?

640
00:47:08,360 --> 00:47:10,029
RUBBER GLOVES

641
00:47:14,992 --> 00:47:16,076
What's this for?

642
00:47:28,797 --> 00:47:32,092
Shower with that on for tonight.
And tomorrow...

643
00:47:32,176 --> 00:47:33,260
Take this off now.

644
00:47:34,678 --> 00:47:35,721
Okay.

645
00:47:36,722 --> 00:47:38,057
I'll take it off.

646
00:47:58,369 --> 00:47:59,536
Oh, Mr. Kang.

647
00:48:01,288 --> 00:48:03,415
Mr. Kang, let me help you.

648
00:48:05,167 --> 00:48:06,168
Are you okay?

649
00:48:08,212 --> 00:48:11,173
Whenever I'm with you,
I have to watch my back and front.

650
00:48:11,256 --> 00:48:12,633
I just can't let my guard down.

651
00:48:14,218 --> 00:48:15,511
I'd better get going.

652
00:48:16,387 --> 00:48:18,764
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

653
00:48:20,724 --> 00:48:23,977
What am I going to do now?
I got into trouble again.

654
00:48:40,619 --> 00:48:41,662
Well...

655
00:48:42,079 --> 00:48:45,499
He just wanted to thank me
for being his fan for so long.

656
00:48:45,833 --> 00:48:49,253
We had dinner at his house.
That's all.

657
00:48:49,336 --> 00:48:51,088
Wait, you went to his house?

658
00:48:51,713 --> 00:48:53,590
How can you say
that's not a big deal?

659
00:48:53,799 --> 00:48:57,803
Normally, you would've made a scene
saying you couldn't believe it.

660
00:48:58,303 --> 00:48:59,430
But why are you so calm?

661
00:49:00,973 --> 00:49:03,016
- You're suspicious.
- You're suspicious.

662
00:49:06,228 --> 00:49:08,188
No, I'm not.

663
00:49:09,148 --> 00:49:11,817
I couldn't be happier.
I'm on cloud nine.

664
00:49:13,944 --> 00:49:18,031
When you experience
something completely unbelievable

665
00:49:18,532 --> 00:49:21,118
you become surprisingly calm.

666
00:49:25,080 --> 00:49:27,458
If that's the case,
I'm happy for you.

667
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:29,334
I was worried for nothing.

668
00:49:35,007 --> 00:49:37,593
Did you see Namda's terrible acting?

669
00:49:40,304 --> 00:49:41,430
Something happened for sure.

670
00:49:42,097 --> 00:49:43,140
Something happened to her.

671
00:49:43,223 --> 00:49:45,142
She was excited to meet Chan.

672
00:49:46,143 --> 00:49:47,853
What the heck happened?

673
00:50:08,790 --> 00:50:10,792
I wonder if Mr. Kang is okay.

674
00:50:15,923 --> 00:50:19,009
He'd think I'm a total nuisance.

675
00:50:21,762 --> 00:50:25,140
He wouldn't use those red gloves.
What was I thinking?

676
00:50:25,224 --> 00:50:26,600
I'm such an idiot.

677
00:50:52,459 --> 00:50:55,170
So what happened to your arm?

678
00:50:55,254 --> 00:50:56,672
It was fine until the weekend.

679
00:50:56,755 --> 00:50:58,173
A dog came at me.

680
00:50:58,590 --> 00:51:01,468
How big was the dog
to leave your arm like that?

681
00:51:08,809 --> 00:51:09,810
Well, it was

682
00:51:11,353 --> 00:51:12,688
about the size of a Pomeranian.

683
00:51:12,771 --> 00:51:14,982
A Pomeranian?

684
00:51:15,857 --> 00:51:17,442
You mean a Pomeranian?

685
00:51:17,526 --> 00:51:18,527
Mr. Kang.

686
00:51:18,860 --> 00:51:20,112
We have a seat for you here.

687
00:51:21,321 --> 00:51:22,990
Come on. Join us.

688
00:51:27,160 --> 00:51:28,245
Have a seat.

689
00:51:31,832 --> 00:51:35,210
Excuse me. We'll get beef brisket
doenjang soup and jeyuk.

690
00:51:35,294 --> 00:51:36,336
Okay.

691
00:51:37,879 --> 00:51:39,214
Mr. Kang, your arm...

692
00:51:40,465 --> 00:51:42,634
Mr. Kang, what happened to your arm?

693
00:51:42,718 --> 00:51:43,927
Let me tell you what happened.

694
00:51:44,011 --> 00:51:46,346
A Pomeranian attacked his arm.

695
00:51:46,430 --> 00:51:48,724
- A Pomeranian?
- Yes, a Pomeranian.

696
00:51:48,807 --> 00:51:51,226
- The small dog?
- Yes, the small dog.

697
00:51:52,144 --> 00:51:54,146
- The cute one?
- Very cute.

698
00:51:54,229 --> 00:51:56,315
A lovely Pomeranian?

699
00:51:56,398 --> 00:51:58,191
The lovely Pomeranian.

700
00:52:03,113 --> 00:52:05,198
I fell.

701
00:52:06,074 --> 00:52:09,953
It must be uncomfortable, Mr. Kang.

702
00:52:10,996 --> 00:52:13,457
Still, you're lucky
it's your left arm

703
00:52:13,540 --> 00:52:14,916
not your right arm.

704
00:52:15,500 --> 00:52:16,668
I'm left-handed.

705
00:52:17,169 --> 00:52:19,588
Oh, I see.

706
00:52:20,631 --> 00:52:22,758
Let's eat.

707
00:52:22,841 --> 00:52:24,551
- Enjoy.
- Enjoy your meal.

708
00:52:29,806 --> 00:52:32,517
Oh, no. What do we do?

709
00:52:33,268 --> 00:52:34,728
- Here.
- Thank you.

710
00:52:34,811 --> 00:52:36,188
I'm worried.

711
00:52:40,817 --> 00:52:42,694
Mr. Kang.

712
00:52:42,861 --> 00:52:44,446
Do you want me to feed you?

713
00:52:46,823 --> 00:52:48,158
No, thank you.

714
00:52:48,241 --> 00:52:50,577
You're eating nothing but rice.

715
00:52:50,869 --> 00:52:51,870
I like rice.

716
00:52:51,953 --> 00:52:54,164
No, let me feed you. Here.

717
00:53:25,570 --> 00:53:31,118
Mr. Kang, the overseas VC wants
to hear back from us by today.

718
00:53:31,201 --> 00:53:32,619
If you confirm it

719
00:53:32,703 --> 00:53:34,746
I'll send the file now.
What do you think?

720
00:53:34,830 --> 00:53:36,248
I want to fix a few pages.

721
00:53:36,915 --> 00:53:37,999
Give me a few minutes.

722
00:53:38,542 --> 00:53:39,543
Bye.

723
00:53:58,562 --> 00:53:59,563
Shoot.

724
00:54:08,363 --> 00:54:09,406
APPELLO CEO KANG HA-GI

725
00:54:10,073 --> 00:54:14,661
Mr. Kang, I'm sorry about all the...

726
00:54:16,163 --> 00:54:17,456
No.

727
00:54:18,874 --> 00:54:19,958
What should I say?

728
00:54:23,462 --> 00:54:27,340
Mr. Kang, if you need anything,
call me anytime...

729
00:54:28,550 --> 00:54:30,135
No.

730
00:54:31,595 --> 00:54:33,930
Why do I keep causing Mr. Kang harm

731
00:54:34,014 --> 00:54:36,850
and nothing ever works out
when I'm with him?

732
00:54:38,518 --> 00:54:39,936
What should I say in the apology?

733
00:54:42,939 --> 00:54:46,151
Think. Think with your brain.

734
00:54:48,987 --> 00:54:49,988
CALLING APPELLO CEO KANG HA-GI

735
00:54:51,823 --> 00:54:52,824
INCOMING CALL
MS. NAM DA-REUM

736
00:55:01,875 --> 00:55:02,876
Hello?

737
00:55:04,753 --> 00:55:05,754
Hello?

738
00:55:06,463 --> 00:55:07,464
Ms. Nam?

739
00:55:08,799 --> 00:55:09,883
Ms. Nam Da-reum?

740
00:55:11,760 --> 00:55:13,970
Yes, Mr. Kang.

741
00:55:14,054 --> 00:55:15,388
You must be off work by now.

742
00:55:15,514 --> 00:55:17,808
Yes. What are you calling me for
at this hour?

743
00:55:19,142 --> 00:55:20,685
Well, that's...

744
00:55:23,605 --> 00:55:25,524
Your arm must be causing you
a lot of discomfort.

745
00:55:25,857 --> 00:55:28,276
I meant to text you
because I was concerned.

746
00:55:28,360 --> 00:55:30,529
But somehow I ended up calling you.

747
00:55:31,696 --> 00:55:34,032
Yes, it's very uncomfortable.

748
00:55:36,243 --> 00:55:37,452
Because of my arm

749
00:55:38,495 --> 00:55:40,288
I couldn't even fix
the urgent proposal.

750
00:55:41,998 --> 00:55:43,083
Really?

751
00:55:45,502 --> 00:55:47,379
That's not good.

752
00:55:47,462 --> 00:55:49,256
I'll go to your house now.

753
00:55:49,339 --> 00:55:51,466
- We live in the same neighborhood.
- What?

754
00:55:52,717 --> 00:55:53,760
But...

755
00:55:54,761 --> 00:55:56,680
You could just help me
at a cafe nearby...

756
00:55:56,763 --> 00:55:58,557
No, you have an injured arm.

757
00:55:58,640 --> 00:56:01,059
How would you bring your laptop
and materials with you?

758
00:56:02,143 --> 00:56:04,229
Just wait. I'll leave soon.

759
00:56:04,312 --> 00:56:05,438
Ms. Nam Da-reum. Nam...

760
00:56:05,730 --> 00:56:07,274
Ms. Nam... Ms. Nam?

761
00:56:18,535 --> 00:56:19,661
Shoot.

762
00:56:38,263 --> 00:56:41,308
This is my chance to make up
for being a nuisance.

763
00:56:41,725 --> 00:56:43,810
Mr. Kang, just wait.

764
00:56:43,894 --> 00:56:46,187
My 600-character-per-minute fingers
are coming.

765
00:56:50,567 --> 00:56:53,111
This is Ha-gi's favorite wine.

766
00:57:03,288 --> 00:57:04,539
I'm here.

767
00:57:09,044 --> 00:57:11,463
Mr. Kang, I'm here.

768
00:57:12,839 --> 00:57:13,840
Okay.

769
00:57:21,765 --> 00:57:24,768
- Hello.
- Ms. Nam.

770
00:57:25,185 --> 00:57:26,895
- That was fast.
- Yes.

771
00:57:27,395 --> 00:57:29,481
Your house is so close.

772
00:57:29,564 --> 00:57:31,483
It's only 500m away from my house.

773
00:57:33,068 --> 00:57:34,819
- Did you run here?
- Yes.

774
00:57:35,070 --> 00:57:36,446
You need to send the proposal soon.

775
00:57:52,295 --> 00:57:53,922
Oh, thank you.

776
00:57:58,677 --> 00:58:00,470
- Where do you want me to work on it?
- What?

777
00:58:02,430 --> 00:58:05,016
Here. No, there.

778
00:58:05,100 --> 00:58:07,394
Oh, how about next to your laptop?

779
00:58:33,003 --> 00:58:35,755
- Mr. Kang, are you okay?
- Yes, I'm okay.

780
00:58:40,218 --> 00:58:41,678
- Mr. Kang.
- Yes?

781
00:58:42,303 --> 00:58:43,346
Is this the one?

782
00:58:44,848 --> 00:58:46,433
Oh, yes.

783
00:58:46,766 --> 00:58:47,767
Then...

784
00:58:50,020 --> 00:58:52,230
It's inconvenient
to look at the monitors this way.

785
00:58:53,356 --> 00:58:54,649
I'll move next to you.

786
00:59:07,162 --> 00:59:08,705
What do you need to add?

787
00:59:12,751 --> 00:59:14,252
- Mr. Kang?
- Yes?

788
00:59:15,211 --> 00:59:16,379
Did you hear what I said?

789
00:59:17,255 --> 00:59:18,465
You need to tell me what to add.

790
00:59:19,924 --> 00:59:21,217
Oh, yes. Right.

791
00:59:22,969 --> 00:59:25,346
- How did I miss that?
- Focus.

792
00:59:26,473 --> 00:59:27,474
Okay.

793
00:59:28,391 --> 00:59:29,392
Focus.

794
00:59:30,602 --> 00:59:33,063
I wanted to add some data
to the original pitch deck.

795
00:59:33,146 --> 00:59:36,274
The CEO of this VC considers
CSR important.

796
00:59:37,650 --> 00:59:40,278
Are you trying to emphasize

797
00:59:40,361 --> 00:59:41,821
Appello's mission of mutual growth?

798
00:59:42,697 --> 00:59:44,449
Yes, that's correct.

799
00:59:44,657 --> 00:59:48,244
Then, how about using the last
online fashion show as an example?

800
00:59:50,580 --> 00:59:52,791
It has a visual impact

